WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.570
Model Context Protocol, often shortened to MCP,

00:00:02.570 --> 00:00:07.156
is a protocol pattern for connecting AI applications to external tools, data, resources,

00:00:07.156 --> 00:00:07.861
and services.

00:00:07.861 --> 00:00:09.625
The core idea is simple:

00:00:09.625 --> 00:00:13.859
an AI system is more useful when it can work with relevant

00:00:13.859 --> 00:00:16.681
context and approved capabilities outside the model itself.

00:00:16.681 --> 00:00:21.267
Instead of every AI application inventing a different integration style, MCP gives hosts,

00:00:21.267 --> 00:00:25.853
clients, and servers a more consistent way to describe and use external capabilities.

00:00:25.853 --> 00:00:30.792
A model is the component that generates or reasons over text and other inputs.

00:00:30.792 --> 00:00:35.731
An AI application is the product or environment that wraps the model for users.

00:00:35.731 --> 00:00:40.318
An agent is an application pattern where the system may plan, select tools,

00:00:40.318 --> 00:00:42.434
and take steps toward a task.

00:00:42.434 --> 00:00:45.257
An integration connects the application to another system.

00:00:45.257 --> 00:00:49.490
An MCP connection is one structured way to expose those integrations so

00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:51.607
the AI application can discover resources,

00:00:51.607 --> 00:00:54.782
call tools, or use prompt templates under defined rules.

00:00:54.782 --> 00:00:59.015
MCP is often compared to a standard integration layer for AI applications

00:00:59.015 --> 00:01:03.249
because it separates the AI experience from the mechanics of each external

00:01:03.249 --> 00:01:03.899
system.

00:01:03.899 --> 00:01:08.838
A developer tool, a documentation source, a ticketing platform, a file system, a database,

00:01:08.838 --> 00:01:14.482
or an internal API can be exposed through a server with capabilities the host can understand.

00:01:14.482 --> 00:01:18.363
That does not mean every capability is automatically safe or appropriate.

00:01:18.363 --> 00:01:22.597
It means the integration surface can be made more consistent and governable.

00:01:22.597 --> 00:01:26.477
Developers care about MCP because it can reduce repeated integration work.

00:01:26.477 --> 00:01:29.652
Security teams care because it makes data flow, permissions,

00:01:29.652 --> 00:01:32.475
and tool use easier to inventory and review.

00:01:32.475 --> 00:01:36.002
Operations teams care because connected tools need ownership, logging, reliability,

00:01:36.002 --> 00:01:37.061
and incident response.

00:01:37.061 --> 00:01:42.353
Product teams care because MCP can make AI features more useful without hard-coding every connection.

00:01:42.353 --> 00:01:45.880
The most important habit is to understand MCP as architecture,

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:47.700
not merely as a plugin feature.
